  Exercise(id:"python-c0-t7-project-4-v1", topic:"python-c0-t7", category:"Project", type:"code", title:"Functions and Variables: mock summary utility", prompt:"Define failure_percent(total, failed) returning the percentage for a positive total. Define main() to read a target label, a positive integer total, and a failed count between zero and total. Strip/lowercase the target. Output Target: NAME, Total: N, Failed: M, Failure rate: P% on four lines; P has two decimals. Call main only through the standard main guard. This is mock data; no files or network requests are required. Explain two cases in My Notes.", tests:[{"input":["  EXAMPLE.ORG ","20","3"],"expected":"Target: example.org\nTotal: 20\nFailed: 3\nFailure rate: 15.00%","harness":"import ast,math\nassert callable(globals().get('failure_percent')), 'Define failure_percent(total, failed).'\nassert math.isclose(failure_percent(4,1),25), 'Return the calculated percentage.'\nassert callable(globals().get('main')), 'Define main().'\ntree=ast.parse(_academy_source)\ndef guard(node):\n    if not isinstance(node,ast.If) or not isinstance(node.test,ast.Compare) or len(node.test.ops)!=1 or not isinstance(node.test.ops[0],ast.Eq):\n        return False\n    values=[node.test.left,*node.test.comparators]\n    return any(isinstance(v,ast.Name) and v.id=='__name__' for v in values) and any(isinstance(v,ast.Constant) and v.value=='__main__' for v in values)\nassert any(guard(n) for n in tree.body), 'Use the standard main guard.'","comparison":"normalized"},{"input":["DEMO","4","0"],"expected":"Target: demo\nTotal: 4\nFailed: 0\nFailure rate: 0.00%","harness":"import ast,math\nassert callable(globals().get('failure_percent')), 'Define failure_percent(total, failed).'\nassert math.isclose(failure_percent(4,1),25), 'Return the calculated percentage.'\nassert callable(globals().get('main')), 'Define main().'\ntree=ast.parse(_academy_source)\ndef guard(node):\n    if not isinstance(node,ast.If) or not isinstance(node.test,ast.Compare) or len(node.test.ops)!=1 or not isinstance(node.test.ops[0],ast.Eq):\n        return False\n    values=[node.test.left,*node.test.comparators]\n    return any(isinstance(v,ast.Name) and v.id=='__name__' for v in values) and any(isinstance(v,ast.Constant) and v.value=='__main__' for v in values)\nassert any(guard(n) for n in tree.body), 'Use the standard main guard.'","comparison":"normalized"},{"input":["mock","3","1"],"expected":"Target: mock\nTotal: 3\nFailed: 1\nFailure rate: 33.33%","harness":"import ast,math\nassert callable(globals().get('failure_percent')), 'Define failure_percent(total, failed).'\nassert math.isclose(failure_percent(4,1),25), 'Return the calculated percentage.'\nassert callable(globals().get('main')), 'Define main().'\ntree=ast.parse(_academy_source)\ndef guard(node):\n    if not isinstance(node,ast.If) or not isinstance(node.test,ast.Compare) or len(node.test.ops)!=1 or not isinstance(node.test.ops[0],ast.Eq):\n        return False\n    values=[node.test.left,*node.test.comparators]\n    return any(isinstance(v,ast.Name) and v.id=='__name__' for v in values) and any(isinstance(v,ast.Constant) and v.value=='__main__' for v in values)\nassert any(guard(n) for n in tree.body), 'Use the standard main guard.'","comparison":"normalized"}], hints:["Separate calculation from the input/output interface."], required:false, filename:"main.py", solution:"def failure_percent(total,failed):\n    return failed/total*100\ndef main():\n    target=input().strip().lower()\n    total=int(input())\n    failed=int(input())\n    print(f\"Target: {target}\")\n    print(f\"Total: {total}\")\n    print(f\"Failed: {failed}\")\n    print(f\"Failure rate: {failure_percent(total,failed):.2f}%\")\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\nOne valid implementation. Compare the result with every supplied case."),
